# Copy to ~/.zshrc.local and edit for this machine.
# Never committed — credentials, internal endpoints and per-machine paths
# belong here, not in the tracked zshrc.
#
# Sourced last by ~/.zshrc, so anything set here overrides the shared config.

# ── Internal / corporate API gateways ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Pi reads these for any gateway defined in pi/models.json with an
# "!printenv VAR" style apiKey. Keep the real variable names and values local.
# export SOME_GATEWAY_API_KEY="..."

# ── AWS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prefer SSO over exported keys:
#     aws sso login --profile <profile>
#     export AWS_PROFILE=<profile>
#
# Temporary STS keys (ASIA...) expire within hours and silently take precedence
# over AWS_PROFILE and SSO, which makes Bedrock and other AWS calls look broken.
# If you must paste them, unset them once they expire:
#     unset AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
# export AWS_PROFILE="..."
